88659 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16195655</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McRae</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Young</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamilton</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Resistance, humidity and temperature of the tracheal airway</article-title><source>Clin Otolaryngol</source><year>1995</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>355</fpage><lpage>356</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1365-2273.1995.tb00059.x</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">McRae RD, Jones AS, Young P, Hamilton J (1995) Resistance, humidity and temperature of the tracheal airway. Clin Otolaryngol 20:355&#x02013;356. doi:10.1111/j.1365-2273.1995.tb00059.x <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8548971</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mercke</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Toremalm</surname><given-names>NG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Air humidity and mucociliary activity</article-title><source>Ann Otol Rhinol Laryngol</source><year>1976</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>32</fpage><lpage>37</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Mercke U, Toremalm NG (1976) Air humidity and mucociliary activity. Ann Otol Rhinol Laryngol 85:32&#x02013;37 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1259315</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="other">Rathgeber J, Zuchner K (1999) Foundations of artificial respiration. Manual for medical docters and nurses. Aktiv Druck &#x00026; Verlag GmbH, Ebelsbach</citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group per