M, van Leeuwen J, Sinaasappel M, Hilgers FJ (2007) A newly developed tool for intra-tracheal temperature and humidity assessment in laryngectomized individuals: the airway climate explorer (ACE). Med Biol Eng Comput 45:737&#x02013;745. doi:10.1007/s11517-007-0217-7 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17629761</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR13"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zuur</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>Muller</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Sinaasappel</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hart</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Zandwijk</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Hilgers</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Influence of heat and moisture exchanger respiratory load on transcutaneous oxygenation in laryngectomized individuals: a randomized crossover study</article-title><source>Head Neck</source><year>2007</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>1102</fpage><lpage>1110</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/hed.20643</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Zuur JK, Muller SH, Sinaasappel M, Hart GA, Van Zandwijk N, Hilgers FJ (2007) Influence of heat and moisture exchanger respiratory load on transcutaneous oxygenation in laryngectomized individuals: a randomized crossover study. Head Neck 29:1102&#x02013;1110. doi:10.1002/hed.20643 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17786991</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zuur</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>Muller</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Vincent</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Sinaasappel</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jongh</surname><given-names>FH</given-names></name><name><surname>Hilgers</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assessment of tracheal temperature and humidity in laryngectomized individuals and the influence of a heat and moisture exchanger on tracheal climate</article-title><source>Head Neck</source><year>2008</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>1072</fpage><lpage>1082</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/hed.20835</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Zuur JK, Muller SH, Vincent A, Sinaasappel M, de Jongh FH, Hilgers FJ (2008) Assessment of tracheal temperature and humidity in laryngectomized individuals and the influence of a heat and moisture exchanger on tracheal climate. Head Neck 30:1072&#x02013;1082. doi:10.1002/hed.20835 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18528903</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>